---
description: WordPress and WooCommerce plugin rules
globs: ["**/*.php"]
---

This project is a custom WordPress / WooCommerce plugin for trefik.nl.

Rules:

- Only modify files inside this plugin
- Never modify WordPress core, WooCommerce core, themes, or other plugins

- Follow PSR-4
- Follow PSR-12

- Respect the autoloader in ./src/Autoloader.php
- Namespace root is Trefik\
- All classes must be loaded from ./includes

- Prefer hooks, filters, and WooCommerce extension points over overrides
- Prefer extending existing behavior over replacing core behavior

- Existing WooCommerce integration classes may act as hook containers
- Before adding new WooCommerce behavior, first check whether there is already:
  - an existing integration class
  - an existing hook registration method
  - an existing register_hooks() entry point

- Avoid duplicating checkout/cart/order logic in a second class if existing WooCommerce integration classes already cover that concern

- Always:
  - Sanitize input
  - Escape output
  - Use nonces where needed
  - Check capabilities where needed

- Respect WooCommerce lifecycle:
  - cart initialization
  - session availability
  - checkout validation
  - order creation
  - thank you page / post-checkout flow

- Keep changes minimal and targeted
- Do not refactor large parts unless explicitly requested

- Be especially careful with:
  - Checkout flow
  - Cart logic
  - Orders
  - Product data
  - User account related flows
  - Email hooks
  - AJAX-driven cart/checkout updates

- Maintain compatibility with existing plugin behavior

- Never introduce direct database manipulation for WooCommerce entities when WooCommerce APIs exist
- Use WooCommerce / WordPress APIs for orders, carts, notices, meta and settings

- Do not assume that a WooCommerce-related class is active unless you verify that it is actually registered in the plugin bootstrap